# App Router pages and components

- Next.js 16 has breaking changes: check `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` before unfamiliar APIs.
- Server Components by default; `'use client'` only on the smallest interactive leaf. No async Client Components.
- Pages: `requireRequestContext()`, await `params`/`searchParams` (Promises), call services directly.
- Client files may import `@/server/actions` only. Never import services, repositories, `@/server/http`, or `@/db`. Props are minimal serializable DTOs.
- No hardcoded KPI numbers or demo strings; unbuilt pages use `ComingNext`.
- Handle loading, empty, unavailable (`unavailableLabel`), forbidden, not-found, and failed states. Show `—`, never `0`, for missing values.
- Format with `src/lib/format.ts` / `src/lib/analytics/display.ts`, not ad-hoc `toFixed`.
- Metadata via `metadata`/`generateMetadata`; never `next/head`.

Full guidance: `.cursor/skills/facilityiq-nextjs-app-router/SKILL.md`, `facilityiq-ui-design-system`, `facilityiq-ui-states-and-forms`.
